Ticket #4471 was treated as one parser defect. The export shows two different failure modes,
so one merged ticket hides a separate booking-form bug. We split the unique reports by tenant
locale, booking form and channel rather than trusting intake's guessed tag.

## Report split

<CauseSplit />

## The two problems

### `parser` — shared parser assumes month first

Day-first tenants send dates in day/month order, but the shared parser reads every date
month-first. The day and month swap, affecting app, email and form reports. This is the larger
group and needs its own engineering ticket: [#1 · 379 reports](https://github.com/ghlmgdv/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1).

### `hint` — booking-v3 shows the wrong date order

For day-first tenants using booking-v3, the date field tells people to enter `MM/DD/YYYY`.
People follow that hint, while the form interprets dates in the tenant's day-first order. This
is a separate form defect, limited to booking-v3 form reports, and needs its own ticket.
The desk tracks it as [#2 · 33 reports](https://github.com/ghlmgdv/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2).

## Triage rule

Use the tenant's configured locale and booking form to assign cause. Do not use the browser
locale or intake tag as the source of truth: the export has reports whose intake tag disagrees
with the cause found from tenant and form data. Count each report ID once because the ticket
export contains overlapping pages.

